# oracle: fix gcmc with CO2 molecules, fix rigid/small and kspace ewald with G-ewald chosen from the accuracy (examples/mc/in.gcmc.co2, shortened): native chooses G-ewald and kmax at the run's init only (Ewald::init) and the trials refresh only the charge sums (KSpace::qsum_qsq), so the inserted and deleted molecules leave G-ewald as it was
# oracle-inputs: w699gcmc_co2.txt
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 abs=1e-14
# measured: the case passes at rel=1e-12 abs=1e-14 (tightest tested); without the frozen G-ewald the step 20 temp differs at 5e-6. The run takes about 1.5 s
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long  14
pair_modify     mix arithmetic tail yes
kspace_style    ewald 0.0001
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     harmonic
lattice         sc 5.0
region          box block 0 10 0 10 0 10 units box
create_box      2 box bond/types 1 angle/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 2 extra/angle/per/atom 1 extra/special/per/atom 2
molecule        co2mol w699gcmc_co2.txt
create_atoms    0 box mol co2mol 464563 units box
pair_coeff      1   1  0.053649   2.8
pair_coeff      2   2  0.156973   3.05
bond_coeff      1       0       1.16
angle_coeff     1       0       180
mass 1 12.0107
mass 2 15.9994
group           co2 type 1 2
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 10 check yes
velocity        all create 338.0 54654
timestep        1.0
fix             myrigid co2 rigid/small molecule mol co2mol
fix_modify      myrigid dynamic/dof yes
fix             mygcmc co2 gcmc 20 20 0 0 54341 338.0 -8.1 0.5 mol co2mol tfac_insert 1.6666666666666667 group co2 rigid myrigid
compute_modify  thermo_temp dynamic/dof yes
thermo_style    custom step temp press pe ke atoms elong f_mygcmc[3] f_mygcmc[4] f_mygcmc[5] f_mygcmc[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
run             100
